  "comment": "Lives in system/ (plumbing). Kernel files that `system/update.mjs` may refresh: this list, plus any path an incoming release lists. Everything else is user data; beyond the listed files update.mjs does only the fixed steps described in its own header (folder moves of the 0.7 layout, the 0.8 business layout, create-once files) and the 0.9 transition in system/migrate-0.9.mjs (its own narrow allowlist, a state file, deletions only after the customer's yes). It refuses any path under user/, business/, areas/, _inbox/ whatever a manifest asks, backs up every file it changes to .aios-backup/, refuses absolute/.. /symlink paths, and will not downgrade. sha256 = as-shipped baseline so an update can detect a kernel file the user edited (conflict -> backup, then overwrite on --apply, never silent). Paths relative to the AIOS root. Regenerate with scripts/gen-managed.mjs after editing any kernel file.",
